@startuml FIG-CL-TAV-06
skinparam shadowing false
title FIG-CL-TAV-06 Diagnostic sequence\nSysML 1.6 notation-based views; executable/metamodel conformance is not claimed\nfailure, overlapping observation, preparatory action, later distinguishing test

actor Operator
participant "Msess" as S
participant "Mprot" as P
participant "Analysis / Diagnosis" as A

Operator -> S : start session, H0 = {h_normal} union H_single
S -> S : overlapping {a,b}/{a,c} stays strictly-reducing even if s(t)=|H|
note right of S
  Worst-case non-shrinkage is not
  "no diagnostic value".
end note
S -> S : Admit; uninformative TEST has no strictly-reducing outcome
S -> S : Select Prep from A, not the uninformative test
S -> P : Prep action through FIG-CL-TAV-04 ports
P --> S : qk+1
S -> S : Select later distinguishing test tb from A
S -> P : Execute tb
P --> S : observation that splits h1 / h2
S -> A : Izk of tb
A --> S : Hk singleton or still indistinguishable
note over S, A
  Prep is a session action in the same admissible set.
  It spends the same selected-mode resource as a test.
  ERROR with unknown-effect does not keep q; recover first.
end note
@enduml
